    "category": "personal",
    "tagline": "Ticket booking built for the rush, when thousands of people want the same seat in the same second.",
    "problem": "When a big show opens for booking, thousands of people click the same seats at once. Without the right locking, two people pay for one seat, or the site falls over under the rush.",
    "description": "Browse movies, stand-up and theatre, pick seats on a live map and hold them while you pay. A Spring Boot API guards every seat with a Redis lock plus optimistic versioning in PostgreSQL, Kafka fans out confirmations, and a Python AI agent answers questions and holds seats from chat.",
